# Style Guide - HTML/SCSS Standards

## SCSS Guidelines
* Prefer Tailwind 2.x when styling components
* Use SCSS with proper nesting (max 3 levels deep)
* Create reusable mixins for common patterns
* Use functions for calculations and transformations
* Organize SCSS with @import statements
* Use partial files (_filename.scss) for modularity
* Utilize variables from `_variables.scss` for breakpoints, colours etc.

## BEM Convention
* Use BEM CSS convention with proper naming:
  * Block: `.wallet-card`
  * Element: `.wallet-card__header`
  * Modifier: `.wallet-card--active`
* Use kebab-case for class names
* Keep class names descriptive and semantic
* Avoid deep nesting in BEM (max 2 levels)

## Accessibility Standards
* Add accessibility attributes (aria-label, aria-describedby)
* Ensure proper color contrast ratios (4.5:1 minimum)
* Use correct semantic HTML elements (button, nav, main, etc.)
* Provide focus indicators for keyboard navigation
* Support screen readers with proper ARIA roles
* Test with keyboard-only navigation

## Responsive Design
* Implement breakpoints consistently
* Use Tailwind for breakpoint definition
* Test on multiple screen sizes
* Use relative units (rem, em, %) over fixed units
* Ensure touch targets are at least 40px

## Performance & Best Practices
* Avoid inline styles, unless angular style bindings
* Use CSS custom properties for dynamic values
* Minimize CSS bundle size
* Use CSS containment where appropriate
* Optimize critical rendering path

## Component Styling
* Use material components
* Create component-specific SCSS files
* Use :host selector for component styles
* Implement proper encapsulation
* Use Angular's class binding for dynamic tyles
* Follow consistent spacing and typography scales

## Design System
* Use design tokens for consistency
* Implement consistent spacing scale
* Use typography scale for font sizes
* Create reusable component patterns
* Maintain visual hierarchy
